  annotation = {中文辅助译名：ENSO与大洋上层热力变化及西北太平洋副热带高压的关系},
  abstract = {The relationships between Southeprn Oscillation Index (SOI), area index of the subtropical high pressure over western pacific (ST)and heat content of the oceanic upper layer in the tropical northwest Pacific (HC)were discussed by using method of spectral analyses. In this paper ,the HC is defined as number of grid -point at which the averaged temperature (TAV)from the sea surface to 100 meter depth is above or equal to 27℃ (i.e. TAV≥27℃ ).Power-spectral analyses show that during 1964-1982,variations in the SOI.STand HC have a similar self-oscillation rhythm and common spectral peak (period for 3 to 4 years ).Cross-spectral analyses between the SOI and HC.and between the ST and HC show significant coherence in these spectral peaks.The SOI leads the HC by two months , and the HC leads the ST by about 6 months .The SOI is in phase with the HC,and the ST is out of phase with the HC.},
}

